 - visual consistency; we've grown a few different "looks": stone
   buttons, the chronicle/howto gold navigation, and the daily's fancy
   card. Should we try to settle on a more consistent look? There are
   some smaller things, too, like some dialog backgrounds (especially
   dailies) having different looks.
 - consider whether chalk should coexist with suppose mode
   - chalk might still be useful for small conjectures and multiplayer
     discussion.
   - consider converting existing chalk into a supposition (the existing
     button could appear only when there's chalk)
   - if chalk is retired, consider using shift-click to enter suppose
     mode
 - custom tiles
   - now that the Halloween tiles are out, we might consider allowing
     you to pick them at will, along with other possible options (e.g.,
     future holiday tiles, or alternate tile sets like Greek letters, or
     others that some may find more readable).
   - one possible mental model: you can pick a pre-made tileset (like
     Halloween), or make your own, picking each row individually. Or
     even design your own row (arbitrary characters? SVG?).
   - if tileset selection gets complicated, it probably needs its own
     dialog off of Options
   - one complication: in multiplayer is a tileset shared, or does
     everyone play with their own (and agree to match if they want to be
     able to discuss)?
 - howto/help improvements
   - tips
     - ordinary puzzles solvable by deduction
     - extreme mode
     - suppose mode
   - online features
     - daily
     - daily scores
     - multiplayer
   - intro tutorial game?
